{"headword":"צְבִי²","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.m.</strong><sup><a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.14\">Is 13:14</a></sup> <strong>gazelle</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.15\">Dt 12:15</a> +; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">צְבָיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.18\">2 S 2:18</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">צְבָאיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:9\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.9\">1 Ch 12:9</a> (Gi Baer; van d. H. v <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:8\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.8\">8</a>), <span dir=\"rtl\">צְבָאוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:7\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.7\">Ct 2:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 3:5\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.3.5\">3:5</a>;—<em>gazelle</em>, allowed as food <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:5\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.5\">Dt 14:5</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.15\">12:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.22\">22</a> (although not for sacrif., Dr; all + <span dir=\"rtl\">אַיָּל</span>), so <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 15:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.15.22\">15:22</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">אַיָּל</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יַחְמוּר</span>, etc.), v. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:3\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.3\">1 K 5:3</a>; sim. of swiftness <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.18\">2 S 2:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:9\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.9\">1 Ch 12:9</a>; v. supr., <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:5\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.5\">Pr 6:5</a>; of grace and beauty <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:9\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.9\">Ct 2:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:17\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.17\">17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:14\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.14\">8:14</a> (cf. Jacob<sup>Arab. Dichter iv. 20 f.</sup>); hence used in adjuration <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:7\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.7\">2:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 3:5\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.3.5\">3:5</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">אילות</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳ מֻדָּח</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.14\">Is 13:14</a>, sim. of fugitives."}]},"rid":"BDB08222","strong_numbers":["6643"],"next_hw":"צְבִיָּה","prev_hw":"צבה²","all_cited":true,"ordinal":"II.","quotes":[],"GK":["7382","7383"],"TWOT":["1869a"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}